 "instruction": "The getter `Status() int` on the `gin.ResponseWriter` interface (response_writer.go) reads like the setter `Context.Status(code int)`, which causes confusion. Rename the interface method `ResponseWriter.Status` to `ResponseStatus`. The rename must cover the interface declaration, every type that implements it, and every call site, including tests. `Context.Status` and any other unrelated `Status` method, field or constant must keep its name. Behavior must not change: the project must still build and its tests must pass.",
 "notes": "Implementer: responseWriter (statically coupled). Look-alikes include Context.Status(code) and http.Response.Status.",
